The model expectations from Hwa and Yang [58] for the most central \(\Omega\) and \(\phi\)\(p_{T}\) spectra are compared to the data in Fig. 4.14. The dashed curves show the \(T_{s}T_{s}T_{s}\) and \(T_{s}T_{s}\) model contributions alone and the solid curves show the sum of all the model contributions. The sum lies on top of the thermal contributions for both particles, highlighting the dominance of recombination of thermal \(s\) quarks to particle production in this framework. (The other model contributions are not shown.) One can see from both panels of Fig. 4.14 that the model shape agrees very well with the experimental values over the measured \(p_{T}\) range for both particles.

